{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f8d8080f94e510bc","type":"text","text":"**Shell (Module 2)**","x":-1080,"y":-880,"width":780,"height":960,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"5cfa2b8d66671d8a","type":"text","text":"EX2\n\n- ***midLS*** list command is  -  \"ls -mtp\":\n  -m adds commas, -t sorts by modified timestamp, -p adds / after directories\n  m or M is important, all the flags are case sensitive\n\n-\n","x":-1060,"y":-320,"width":740,"height":170},
		{"id":"a8db6142a4337445","type":"text","text":"EX3\n\n- for having special characters show up in filenames ***we must unescape them with an \\ symbol***, ie:    \\ !   |   \\ #   |   \\ \\    (without a space, obsidian bypass).\n- \n","x":-1060,"y":-120,"width":740,"height":160},
		{"id":"f0841ada3d34b4cb","type":"text","text":"EX0\n\n- ***truncate -s*** allows to manually change size of a file\n-\n","x":-1060,"y":-820,"width":740,"height":120},
		{"id":"8edcf9122129fa6e","type":"text","text":"EX1\n\n- ***chmod*** permission numbers: 4 - read, 2 write, 1 - execute \n  (for u - user, g - group, o - others)\n- ***chmod perms look like this:***\n  -rwxrwxrwx  as  - (file or dir), rwx (u), rwx (g), rwx (o);\n  (r - read, w - write, x -execute).\n-  number after perms is a link counter, if you link to itself both the file and link will have 2 (think of it as references)\n- ***touch -t*** allows to set date & time in this format: \n  mmddhhmm  -  06012243  -  Jun 01 22:43\n- \n","x":-1060,"y":-680,"width":740,"height":340},
		{"id":"cdd90f63332f621d","type":"text","text":"**Tutorial (Module 1)**","x":-1080,"y":-1200,"width":280,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"2fc84bb85339a97a","type":"text","text":"- No notes available.\n- Only this is to always read man pages CAREFULLY!!","x":-1060,"y":-1140,"width":240,"height":160},
